>> title: Costra de Azúcar
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: topping, mexican, sugar, paste, make-ahead
>> counters: Panadería
>> aka: costra de azucar, costra, concha topping, tapa de concha, sugar paste topping, cookie lid
>> pairs-with: conchas, bigotes-de-pina
>> servings: 16
>> time: 20 min
>> step.1: cream the fats and sugar
>> step.2: work in the flour to a stiff paste
>> step.3: flavour, then divide and tint

Cream @vegetable shortening{1/3%cup}(65 g) and @softened unsalted butter{1/4%cup}(55 g) with @powdered sugar{1 1/4%cup}(150 g) until pale. Shortening is not a shortcut here — it is what keeps the lid from melting into the bun in the oven, and every shop uses it.

Work @all-purpose flour{1 1/4%cup}(150 g) into @&(~1)creamed fat{} until it comes together as a stiff, rollable paste, about the feel of marzipan.

Flavour @&(~1)paste{} with @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), then divide it in three: leave one plain, knead @cocoa powder{1%Tbs}(6 g) into the second and @pink gel food colouring{4%drops} into the third. Vanilla, chocolate and pink strawberry are the three lids in the case; nothing else about them differs.
